  "hints": [
    {
      "tier": "direction",
      "text": "Start with lineTotalCents: check each argument against the rules before you compute anything, and throw as soon as one is wrong."
    },
    {
      "tier": "pattern",
      "text": "subtotalCents is an accumulator loop: start a running total at 0 and add one line per iteration. Reuse lineTotalCents so every line gets the same validation."
    },
    {
      "tier": "key_insight",
      "text": "Most bugs here are boundaries: a loop condition of i < length - 1 skips the last line, and > instead of >= makes a subtotal of exactly 5000 pay shipping."
    },
    {
      "tier": "pseudocode",
      "text": "lineTotal: if price < 0 or quantity < 1 -> throw; return multiplyExact(price, quantity). subtotal: if lengths differ -> throw; total = 0; for i in 0..length-1: total = addExact(total, lineTotal(prices[i], quantities[i])). shipping: if subtotal == 0 or subtotal >= threshold -> 0 else standard fee."
    }
  ],
